      "question_text": "The IUPAC name for",
      "question_html": "<div class=\"q-body\"> <div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p>The IUPAC name for</p>\n<p><img alt=\"KCET 2022 Chemistry - IUPAC Nomenclatures Question 4 English\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1ltbso6t5/37291fb3-9d36-42dd-bcbc-d201f01dd527/a362b690-d984-11ee-bce9-1f4a70aeb3d5/file-6y3zli1ltbso6t6.png\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1ltbso6t5/37291fb3-9d36-42dd-bcbc-d201f01dd527/a362b690-d984-11ee-bce9-1f4a70aeb3d5/file-6y3zli1ltbso6t6.png?format=png\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/6y3zli1ltbso6t5/37291fb3-9d36-42dd-bcbc-d201f01dd527/a362b690-d984-11ee-bce9-1f4a70aeb3d5/file-6y3zli1ltbso6t6.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/6y3zli1ltbso6t5/37291fb3-9d36-42dd-bcbc-d201f01dd527/a362b690-d984-11ee-bce9-1f4a70aeb3d5/file-6y3zli1ltbso6t6.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1ltbso6t5/37291fb3-9d36-42dd-bcbc-d201f01dd527/a362b690-d984-11ee-bce9-1f4a70aeb3d5/file-6y3zli1ltbso6t6.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/6y3zli1ltbso6t5/37291fb3-9d36-42dd-bcbc-d201f01dd527/a362b690-d984-11ee-bce9-1f4a70aeb3d5/file-6y3zli1ltbso6t6.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/6y3zli1ltbso6t5/37291fb3-9d36-42dd-bcbc-d201f01dd527/a362b690-d984-11ee-bce9-1f4a70aeb3d5/file-6y3zli1ltbso6t6.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/6y3zli1ltbso6t5/37291fb3-9d36-42dd-bcbc-d201f01dd527/a362b690-d984-11ee-bce9-1f4a70aeb3d5/file-6y3zli1ltbso6t6.png?format=png 2500w\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\"/></p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div></div>",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "1,4-dioxopentanol",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->1,4-dioxopentanol\n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "1-carboxybutan-3-one",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->1-carboxybutan-3-one\n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "4-oxopentanoic acid",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->4-oxopentanoic acid\n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "1-hydroxy pentane-1, 4-dione",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->1-hydroxy pentane-1, 4-dione<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": null,
      "explanation_text": "The given compound contains a carboxylic acid group (-COOH) and a ketone group (-CO-) within the carbon chain. When naming compounds according to the IUPAC system, priority is given to certain functional groups. The carboxylic acid group has higher priority than the ketone group. Thus, the compound will be named with the suffix \"-oic acid\" to denote the presence of the carboxylic acid. The longest carbon chain that contains the carboxylic acid group has five carbons, so the base name will be \"pentanoic acid.\" The carbon atoms are numbered starting from the carboxylic acid group to give the substituent, in this case, the ketone group, the lowest possible number. The ketone is on the fourth carbon, so it will be indicated with \"4-oxo.\" Therefore, the correct IUPAC name for the compound is \"4-oxopentanoic acid,\" which corresponds to Option C. Options A, B, and D do not correctly prioritize the functional groups nor do they name the compound with proper numbering and suffixes based on IUPAC rules.",
      "explanation_html": "<div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p><img alt=\"KCET 2022 Chemistry - IUPAC Nomenclatures Question 4 English Explanation\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1ltc4nchy/9034f317-e502-4b42-9bc8-69bf01dbabfb/79855a60-d9b3-11ee-983a-35ba8017a6a3/file-6y3zli1ltc4nchz.png\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1ltc4nchy/9034f317-e502-4b42-9bc8-69bf01dbabfb/79855a60-d9b3-11ee-983a-35ba8017a6a3/file-6y3zli1ltc4nchz.png?format=png\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/6y3zli1ltc4nchy/9034f317-e502-4b42-9bc8-69bf01dbabfb/79855a60-d9b3-11ee-983a-35ba8017a6a3/file-6y3zli1ltc4nchz.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/6y3zli1ltc4nchy/9034f317-e502-4b42-9bc8-69bf01dbabfb/79855a60-d9b3-11ee-983a-35ba8017a6a3/file-6y3zli1ltc4nchz.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1ltc4nchy/9034f317-e502-4b42-9bc8-69bf01dbabfb/79855a60-d9b3-11ee-983a-35ba8017a6a3/file-6y3zli1ltc4nchz.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/6y3zli1ltc4nchy/9034f317-e502-4b42-9bc8-69bf01dbabfb/79855a60-d9b3-11ee-983a-35ba8017a6a3/file-6y3zli1ltc4nchz.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/6y3zli1ltc4nchy/9034f317-e502-4b42-9bc8-69bf01dbabfb/79855a60-d9b3-11ee-983a-35ba8017a6a3/file-6y3zli1ltc4nchz.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/6y3zli1ltc4nchy/9034f317-e502-4b42-9bc8-69bf01dbabfb/79855a60-d9b3-11ee-983a-35ba8017a6a3/file-6y3zli1ltc4nchz.png?format=png 2500w\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\"/></p>\n<p>The given compound contains a carboxylic acid group (-COOH) and a ketone group (-CO-) within the carbon chain. When naming compounds according to the IUPAC system, priority is given to certain functional groups. The carboxylic acid group has higher priority than the ketone group. Thus, the compound will be named with the suffix \"-oic acid\" to denote the presence of the carboxylic acid.</p>\n<p>The longest carbon chain that contains the carboxylic acid group has five carbons, so the base name will be \"pentanoic acid.\" The carbon atoms are numbered starting from the carboxylic acid group to give the substituent, in this case, the ketone group, the lowest possible number. The ketone is on the fourth carbon, so it will be indicated with \"4-oxo.\" </p>\n<p>Therefore, the correct IUPAC name for the compound is \"4-oxopentanoic acid,\" which corresponds to Option C. Options A, B, and D do not correctly prioritize the functional groups nor do they name the compound with proper numbering and suffixes based on IUPAC rules.</p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>",
